Z||000000||jhogans||06-12-2000||04:15 PM||||What online rim retailers do you guys recommend?<P>What are the biggest tires I can put on my 86 GT?  I'm looking at getting 17" rims.  I tried doing a search but I kept getting a connection time out. <P>Thanks for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-12-2000||04:28 PM||||There is <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A> <BR>and the <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com." TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com.</A>  <BR>Both of these have a wide selection of wheels and tires. They both have a "Virtual wheel section" so you can see different wheels on the same car but only Tire Rack has a Fiero. (Only a red coupe). You can order wheels and tires together for a "package" price. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||06-12-2000||04:33 PM||||Take a look at the topic, you gotta amke a comment and you can see the wheels and tires I isnstalled. Those are 17" rims with 215/45/17 in front and 235/456/17 in the rear. Thos are according to a computer print out are: in the front, .17 inches bigerr in height then the stock 205/60/15 and the rear is: .31 inches taller then the stock 215/60/15 that came with the car. I have diven the GT with the new wheeks and rims and the car handles really well. Actually better then before. I also have my GT lowered 1 inch.||||reg||1
